{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And I will strike the winter house</b> — Thus is the custom of princes in the land of Ishmael, and similar is בעליית המקרה. R. Marinus said: For בית השן was one house that Ahab made, and he joined to it noble houses, like וכסיליהם, which is one Kesil in the heavens. And I say: If one Kesil is in the heavens, there are many on earth and it is one of them, and in the verse עֹשֶׂה כִימָה וְכְסִיל I will explain this. And if Ahab made one בית שן, others after him made many houses."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Reading כסיל as the constellation Orion throughout; the argument plays on the dual meaning of כסיל as both a stellar name and 'fool.' בעליית המקרה is opaque; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:00.589253250Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}